# Cloudflare Workers static-asset cache policy.
# Without this file the platform default is "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", i.e. no
# real browser caching: styles.css, fonts, and the large JSON shards revalidate on every
# navigation. Durations are kept modest so the monthly data refresh still lands promptly,
# and the post-deploy cache purge already clears the edge on each deploy.
# Note: Workers _headers allows only ONE splat (*) per URL pattern, so each data path is
# listed explicitly rather than /*/data/*.

# Baseline security headers on every response. The CSP is matched to the resources the site
# actually loads: inline <script>/<style> (hence 'unsafe-inline') and the cookieless Cloudflare
# beacon. Since Release 3 B3 the fonts are self-hosted from /fonts, so style-src and font-src no
# longer allow fonts.googleapis.com or fonts.gstatic.com: the only remaining third-party origin is
# the beacon. 'unsafe-inline' is a real weakening, but the pages are static
# and load no third-party scripts beyond the beacon, so the practical risk is low and the
# nosniff/HSTS protections are the meaningful wins. Revisit CSP if inline JS is ever moved out.
#
# Frame protection is done with X-Frame-Options: DENY, NOT a CSP frame-ancestors directive. This
# is deliberate: Cloudflare _headers APPENDS a per-path CSP rather than replacing it, so a global
# `frame-ancestors 'none'` cannot be relaxed on /embed/ (the browser enforces the strictest of the
# two CSPs). X-Frame-Options can be unset per-path with `!`, so it is the mechanism that lets the
# embed widget opt out while every other page stays frame-denied.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), browsing-topics=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# The /embed/ widget is meant to be iframed by other sites (journalists, schools), so it opts OUT
# of the sitewide frame block by unsetting X-Frame-Options. Nothing forbids framing it (the global
# CSP sets no frame-ancestors), so it embeds anywhere; every other page keeps X-Frame-Options: DENY.
# (There is no auth or state-changing action here to clickjack.)
/embed/*
  ! X-Frame-Options

# Stylesheet and icons: change rarely, safe to hold for an hour.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Self-hosted fonts: immutable for a year. Safe because each filename pins the family, weight and
# subset, so a different face is always a different URL. Replace the file name, never the bytes.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Generated data shards (the heavy payloads): one day.
/value-check/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/careers/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/k12/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Downloadable datasets under /data/.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Pre-rendered HTML pages: an hour lets a repeat visitor navigate instantly while still
# picking up the monthly rebuild within the day.
/college/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/colleges/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/majors/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/lists/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
